# Fungi tuft 4: a coral fungus about 0.7 m tall, a thick cream trunk forking into four fat, apricot-orange branches that
# fork again and again into blunt, rounded tips, like a hand held up. Oversized for the forest floor, so it reads at a distance;
# the counterpart of flower4. It barely sways.
format 1

# Detail as the grass and flowers have it: the fine stalks and thin stems are small next to the model's size
